# Accepted findings for the toolchain container image scan (security-scan.yml).
# Each entry needs a reason and a revisit condition; see also SECURITY.md's
# "Known scanner findings (accepted)" section.

# pip's vendored msgpack 1.1.2 (pip 26.2.1, pipx shared venv at
# /home/ubuntu/.local/share/pipx/shared/.../pip/_vendor). Used only by pip
# internally during installs; nothing this project builds imports or links
# it, and the conan venv's real msgpack is upgraded past this (1.2.2).
# Not fixable here: pip pins its vendored set. Revisit when pip re-vendors.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# pip's vendored setuptools 70.3.0, same vendored set as above. The CVE is a
# path traversal in setuptools' PackageIndex, which pip's internal use never
# exercises; the conan venv's real setuptools is upgraded at image build
# time. Not fixable here: pip pins its vendored set. Revisit when pip
# re-vendors.
CVE-2025-47273
